  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provision of lifesaving, GBViE multi-service assistance to Ethiopian Refugees in East Sudan 2022-24</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">D&amp;P, in partnership with CAFOD and NCA, proposes to provide emergency protection assistance to 12,500 Ethiopian women, men and children in Tunaydbah Refugee Settlement. A comprehensive package of services will be provided to at-risk refugees and GBV survivors in NCA&#x2019;s Women and Girls Safe Space and Community Centre, including psychological support and referrals, life skills and recreational activities, and cash assistance. In addition, the project will focus on preventing GBV and other protection risks in the community through outreach activities and awareness raising campaigns as well as through protection-focused multi-sector services such as the provision of energy kits (fuel efficient cooking stoves and portable solar lights) and essential hygiene and sanitation products (including menstrual hygiene). The two-year implementation period will allow to build self-sufficiency and resilience among the target community, especially of women and girls, and to reach sustainable changes by addressing structural inequalities, injustices, and barriers (including GBV-related rights and entitlements). 
It is expected that 12,500 refugees will benefit from multiple services under this project, including 8,401 (80%F/ 20%M) who will benefit directly from protection services over two years. This represents 75% of all females and 25% of all males in the camp.</narrative>
  </description>
